<code>assert \forall String p; this.startsWith(p) && !\old(this.startsWith(p)) => this.countPrefix(p) == \old(this.countPrefix(p)) + 1;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String prefix; this.startsWith(prefix) && !\old(this.startsWith(prefix)) => this.countPrefix(prefix) == \old(this.countPrefix(prefix)) + 1;</code>

This assert statement captures the essence of the comment: when a non-null word that is not already in the trie is added, for each prefix of this word, the number of words extending this prefix in the new trie goes up by 1. The condition checks that the prefix starts with the newly added word and was not present before, ensuring the count increases by 1.
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String p; this.startsWith(p) && !\old(this.startsWith(p)) => this.countPrefix(p) == \old(this.countPrefix(p)) + 1;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int j; 0 <= j && j <= word.length(); \old(this.countPrefix(word.substring(0, j))) + 1 == this.countPrefix(word.substring(0, j)) && !\old(this.contains(word)) && word != null;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall String p; this.startsWith(p) && !\old(this.startsWith(p)) => this.countPrefix(p) == \old(this.countPrefix(p)) + 1;</code>
